WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:06.264
Redness

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:17.304
Facial redness is often caused by hormonal changes, and it comes in two types: plain redness and redness with a warm, flushed feeling.

3
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:25.152
If there's warmth involved, a cooling product needs to be used first to bring that heat down.

4
00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:30.696
That's because the warmth can make foundation lift off the skin.

5
00:00:31.032 --> 00:00:39.672
If it's just mild redness, a color-correcting base is used to neutralize it before the skin finish goes on.

6
00:00:40.008 --> 00:00:47.064
Blush also needs to be applied carefully so it doesn't emphasize the redness further.

7
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.560
Melasma and blemishes

8
00:00:49.896 --> 00:00:57.768
As skin ages, it naturally becomes duller and develops blemishes like melasma and age spots.

9
00:00:58.104 --> 00:01:06.360
Melasma and blemishes can be fully covered with the professional technique of layering thin coats multiple times.

10
00:01:06.696 --> 00:01:11.784
Simply piling on heavy coverage actually makes fine lines stand out more,

11
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:23.784
so it's better to apply a hydrating liquid foundation thinly and layer concealer or a stick product only on the blemishes themselves, keeping the skin looking healthy while covering it naturally.

12
00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:32.736
In other words, rather than piling on coverage for a perfect cover-up, it's enough to simply make blemishes less visible.

13
00:01:33.072 --> 00:01:43.464
Melasma and blemishes are a common concern for many wedding parents, but they can be well managed with a professional's careful touch, so there's no need to worry too much.

14
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:55.560
For the best results, it's essential to start one or two months before the wedding with steady hydration and exfoliation, to build a skin base that makeup can settle into well.

15
00:01:55.896 --> 00:02:06.768
Applying a dewy, subtly glowing baby-face makeup technique naturally covers blemishes and leaves you looking far brighter and more refined.

16
00:02:07.104 --> 00:02:14.256
If you're planning laser treatment to remove melasma, avoid spring or summer when UV rays are strong,

17
00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:23.568
and afterward, take extra care with thorough sun protection and moisturizing to prevent pigmentation from worsening.
